गुरु॑ f. गुर्वी a. heavy, weighty (w. abl. also =
गुरुतर), big, large, great, long (prosod.);
 strong, vehement;
difficult, hard;
 bad, evil;
 important, valuable, venerable. Comp.
गुरुतर & ग॑रीयंस् heavier, weightier, etc. than (abl.);
 very heavy,
weighty etc.;
 superl. गरिष्ठ very big or swollen. — m. any
venerable person, as father, mother (du. the parents), teacher (also
pl.), esp. Brhaspati as the teacher of the gods, any elder relative;
chief of (—˚). f. गुर्वी pregnant, a pregnant woman.

गुरुकुल n. the teacher's house;
 ˚वास m. the living in
it, scholarship.

गुरुतल्प m. the teacher's bed;
 violator or violation of
it.

गुरुत्व n. weight, heaviness, severity;
 prosodical length,
importance etc. = prec.

गुर्वर्थ m. an important affair;
 also the teacher's
affair or fee;
 ˚र्थम् adv. for the parents or the teacher.
